.TH geectl-commit 1  "geectl-commit 0.3.0" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-commit \- Commit the staged changes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl commit\fR [\fB\-\-noservice\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-local\-services\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-server\-services\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-message\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Commit the staged changes
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-message\fR \fI<MESSAGE>\fR
The commit message
.TP
\fB\-\-noservice\fR
Skip the local service gate and the server\-side services: the combined shorthand for `\-\-no\-local\-services` and `\-\-no\-server\-services`
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-local\-services\fR
Skip the local service gate (source services and `pre_checkin.sh`) only; the server still runs its services for the commit
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-server\-services\fR
Skip the server\-side services for the commit only (`noservice=1` on the commit); the local service gate still runs. OBS\-native commits only: a git\-backed commit has no server\-side services switch, so the flag has no effect there
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0
